+---
+id: task-001-fix-lower-case-sku-lookup
+type: task
+title: "Fix lower-case SKU lookup"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Giulia (sales desk) reported that typing a product code in lower case (e.g. `lb-220`) gets refused as
+unknown, while the same code in capitals works.
+
+## Root cause
+
+`Catalog.find` looked up the product map with `sku.trim()` instead of normalising the SKU to its
+canonical upper-case form. Products are stored under their canonical SKU (`canonicalSku`), so any
+lookup that wasn't already upper case missed the map.
+
+## Fix
+
+`src/catalog.ts`: `find()` now looks up with `canonicalSku(sku)` instead of `sku.trim()`, matching how
+products are stored and how `add()` already normalises SKUs.
+
+## Tests
+
+Added a red-first test in `test/catalog.test.ts` ("finds a product by a SKU typed in lower case") that
+adds `LB-220` and looks it up as `lb-220` via both `get` and `getForSale`. It failed before the fix and
+passes after.
