@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+---
+id: task-003-fix-vat-rounding-truncating-instead-of-rounding-half-up
+type: task
+title: "Fix VAT rounding truncating instead of rounding half up"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Accounting reported that some order lines' VAT is one cent lower than expected: a €1.99 line at the
+standard rate (22%) showed €0.43 of VAT instead of €0.44.
+
+## Root cause
+
+The README states VAT is "rounded half up to the cent on each line." `lineVat` in `src/tax.ts` computed
+`Math.floor((net * rate) / 100)`, which truncates instead of rounding half up. For net = 199, rate = 22:
+199 * 22 / 100 = 43.78, which should round up to 44 cents but was truncated to 43.
+
+`shippingVat` in the same file already used `percentOf`, which rounds half up via `divideHalfUp` in
+`src/money.ts`; `lineVat` was the odd one out.
+
+## Fix
+
+`src/tax.ts`: `lineVat` now computes `divideHalfUp(net * vatRate(vatClass), 100)` instead of
+`Math.floor`, reusing the same half-up rounding helper already used for shipping VAT.
+
+## Tests
+
+Added a red-first test in `test/orders.test.ts` ("rounds a line's VAT half up to the cent") with a
+€1.99 standard-rate product, asserting its line VAT is 44 cents. It failed before the fix and passes
+after.
